<title>USA: NYPA shuts 135 MW N.Y. power plant for 6 weeks.</title>
<headline>NYPA shuts 135 MW N.Y. power plant for 6 weeks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Power Authority (NYPA) shut its 135 megawatt (MW) Richard M Flynn power plant for a six-week maintenance outage, a spokeswoman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Output from the station is sold to Long Island Lighting Co.</p>
<p>The Flynn station, which uses either fuel oil or natural gas to produce electricity, is in Holtsville on Long Island, N.Y.</p>
<p>NYPA generates one fourth of the electricity produced in the state of New York.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622</p>
</text>
